Description: Wild OS Report a problem
 Report a problem writes up what went wrong in Wild OS: what happened,
 when, whether it happens again and a screenshot, with the Wild OS
 version and the PC's model, the crash record, the log for that time and
 the recent updates. Names, the PC's name, Wi-Fi names, addresses, serial
 numbers, email addresses and file names are replaced with placeholders
 before anything is shown, and every part can be left out. Nothing is
 sent for you: open an issue on GitHub, save the report or copy the
 description. After Open GitHub it looks for the new issue in GitHub's
 public list of issues, without signing in, to say when it is up.
 .
 After an app crashes, a notice offers to report it, at most once per app
 per day. systemd-coredump records which program crashed, never its
 memory.
